{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"r1","type":"claim","text":"Adopt a shared digital chore board (e.g., Google Sheet or Trello) that lists all recurring tasks and lets each roommate assign themselves weekly, with easy re‑assignment when schedules shift."},{"id":"r2","type":"claim","text":"Hold a brief weekly chore check‑in (around 10 minutes) to review the board, confirm assignments, and negotiate any swaps or overloads."},{"id":"r3","type":"claim","text":"Introduce a non‑verbal cue (e.g., colored stickers or emoji tags on the board) so a roommate can signal they are busy or need help without a direct conversation."},{"id":"r4","type":"objection","text":"If a roommate consistently avoids the weekly check‑in, the group should establish a gentle reminder policy and a fallback redistribution rule to prevent tasks from piling up on others."}],"uptake":[]}